  "description": "CR 611.2a the window follows the Giant to bob, so it cannot attack on his turn",
  "note": "Wall of Dust's \"that creature can't attack during its controller's next turn\" names a window, and \"its controller\" is read when that turn comes (Gideon, Battle-Forged's 2015-06-22 ruling). Wall of Dust blocks alice's Hill Giant on turn 1; on turn 2 bob's Act of Treason takes it, untapped and hasty, so his turn is its controller's next: the Giant is not offered and a declaration with it is refused. The --control board's Wall of Stone, a vanilla defender, blocks the same way and stores nothing, and there the stolen Giant attacks. bob's Grizzly Bears is offered on both so the declaration is asked at all.",
